stem:
A figure in the $xy$-plane is subjected to the following three transformations, one after another, in the order listed:

1. reflection in the line $x = 2$;
2. reflection in the line $y = 3$;
3. rotation through $90^\circ$ anticlockwise about the point $(2, 3)$.

The combined effect on every figure is the same as that of a single transformation. Which one of the following is that single transformation?

